<h1>search</h1>
<p>
(algorithm)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
Look for a value or item in a data structure.  There are dozens of algorithms, data structures, and approaches.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Specialization</strong> (... is a kind of me.)<br>
<a href="binarySearch.html"><em>binary search</em></a>, <a href="linearSearch.html"><em>linear search</em></a>, <a href="stringMatching.html"><em>string matching</em></a>, <a href="depthfirst.html"><em>depth-first search</em></a>, <a href="BondSeqSearch.html"><em>Bond Sequential Search</em></a>, <a href="jumpsearch.html"><em>jump search</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="array.html"><em>array</em></a>, <a href="btree.html"><em>B-tree</em></a>, <a href="dictionary.html"><em>dictionary</em></a>, <a href="hashtab.html"><em>hash table</em></a>, <a href="heap.html"><em>heap</em></a>, <a href="invertedIndex.html"><em>inverted index</em></a>, <a href="linkedList.html"><em>linked list</em></a>, <a href="quadtree.html"><em>quadtree</em></a>, <a href="selectkth.html"><em>select k<sup>th</sup> element</em></a>, <a href="selectAndPartition.html"><em>select and partition</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
For more information, see the data structure in question or <a href="../termsArea.html#search">terms related to searching</a>.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

